      "skill": "brainstorming",
      "metaText": "source: obra/superpowers\nref: main\ncommit: 896224c4b1879920ab573417e68fd51d2ccc9072\nupstream_path: skills/brainstorming\nlocal_path: skills/brainstorming\nfetched_at: 2026-06-27\nnotes: |\n  Local modifications — re-apply these whenever updating from upstream:\n\n  1. description set to \"Manual-only.\" so the skill never auto-triggers. (SKILL.md)\n  2. Terminal state changed: instead of automatically invoking the writing-plans\n     skill after the spec is approved, the fork closes the flow and tells the user\n     brainstorming is complete, leaving the next step to the user. All automatic\n     skill-chaining language removed (writing-plans / frontend-design / etc.).\n     (SKILL.md only — step 9, the flow-diagram terminal node + edge, the\n     \"terminal state\" paragraph, the sub-project line, the scope-check line, the\n     user-review-gate message, and the \"After Approval\" block.)\n  3. De-branded the \"superpowers\" ecosystem:\n     - Spec output path docs/superpowers/specs/ -> docs/specs/\n       (SKILL.md step 6 and the \"After the Design\" section, and\n       spec-document-reviewer-prompt.md).\n     - Visual-companion runtime session directory .superpowers/brainstorm/ ->\n       .brainstorm/ (scripts/start-server.sh path logic + usage comment,\n       scripts/stop-server.sh comment, and visual-companion.md references\n       including the .gitignore hint). scripts/server.cjs needs no change — it\n       receives the directory via env, never hardcodes it.\n     - NOT changed (deliberately left upstream): the \"Superpowers\" UI branding,\n       remote logo, and telemetry env handling in scripts/server.cjs and\n       scripts/frame-template.html. These only render inside the user's own\n       browser tab during a session, so they were judged not worth the\n       script-divergence cost.\n  4. Fixed an internal path reference for the fork's layout: SKILL.md points to\n     the visual companion guide as `visual-companion.md` (its own sibling), not\n     upstream's repo-root `skills/brainstorming/visual-companion.md`, which does\n     not resolve from the installed skill folder.\n\n  Reconciled to the upstream commit above on 2026-06-27: took scripts/,\n  visual-companion.md, and spec-document-reviewer-prompt.md from upstream\n  wholesale, then re-applied the local modifications listed above. This absorbed\n  upstream's session-key auth, the --open flag (kept — orthogonal to manual-only),\n  selection-indicator changes, and the just-in-time visual-companion model. The\n  just-in-time model replaced the older \"Visual questions ahead?\" flow node; that\n  node was upstream's all along (introduced in obra/superpowers and later removed\n  there), NOT a local modification — an earlier note here claimed otherwise and was\n  wrong.\n"
